I find that with Nethack the first 1-7 levels are always too hard and the
rest are too easy.  When beginners get discouraged, it's probably because
they get tired of dying on level 3 or so, not realizing that once they got
a 10th or 11th level character, the rest would be a walk.

Look at standard, old fashioned, version 1.0 non-Ultra Rogue for a dungeon
game that has a good steady increment of difficulty.  Each successive dungeon
level is successively more difficult to survive, and it is a f**in miracle 
if you actually get the amulet.  With Nethack, it's often a miracle if you 
get to level 10 (either dungeon or character), and really a miracle of
stupidity if you get killed thereafter.  I've played a lot, and I really enjoy
playing until ~ level 10 ... perhaps we could make both beginners and
advanced players happier by making the beginning easier and the rest harder.

I know it's tough when an advanced character with time invested in it gets
killed, but right now playing a > Lev 10 character mostly feels like using
an editor right now ... delete the 'D' with a few keystrokes ... delete
the 'U' ... delete the 'H' ... and so on.  And then I get bored, and get 
killed by accident because the game isn't keeping you alert.  And I don't 
use teleport, teleport control, or polypiling.  

